### 1. The "Clean & Safe" Optimization (Recommended)
The original code has a critical flaw: **Infinite Loops**.
If the array contains duplicate values equal to the pivot, the inner `while` loops (`arr[i] < pivot` and `arr[j] > pivot`) will skip over them. If the pointers cross without swapping, the outer loop condition `i <= j` remains true, causing an infinite loop.

Additionally, the original code performs a full swap for every element, which is slow.

Here is the optimized version using **Hoare's Partition Scheme** (which is generally faster than Lomuto) and includes a **Termination Condition** to prevent infinite loops on duplicates.

```java
public class QuickSort {
    public static void quickSort(int[] arr, int low, int high) {
        if (arr == null || arr.length == 0) return;
        if (low < high) {
            int pi = partition(arr, low, high);
            quickSort(arr, low, pi - 1);
            quickSort(arr, pi + 1, high);
        }
    }

    // Optimized Partition Method
    private static int partition(int[] arr, int low, int high) {
        // 1. Pivot Selection: Median-of-Three is better than random or middle
        // to avoid worst-case O(n^2) on sorted arrays.
        int pivotIndex = medianOfThree(arr, low, high);
        int pivotValue = arr[pivotIndex];

        // 2. Move pivot to end for easier swapping
        swap(arr, pivotIndex, high);
        int pivot = high; 

        int i = low - 1; // i points to the last element smaller than pivot

        for (int j = low; j < high; j++) {
            if (arr[j] <= pivotValue) {
                i++;
                swap(arr, i, j);
            }
        }

        // 3. Place pivot in correct position
        swap(arr, i + 1, high);
        return i + 1;
    }

    // Helper: Median of Three (First, Middle, Last)
    private static int medianOfThree(int[] arr, int low, int high) {
        int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
        if (arr[low] > arr[mid]) {
            if (arr[mid] > arr[high]) return mid;
            else if (arr[low] < arr[high]) return high;
            else return low;
        } else {
            if (arr[low] > arr[high]) return high;
            else if (arr[mid] > arr[high]) return high;
            else return low;
        }
    }

    private static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[j];
        arr[j] = temp;
